**PROPOSITION 6.6.** Any two initial $T$-algebras are uniquely isomorphic. $\square$

Slightly more interesting is the behaviour of $T$ on initial algebras.

The [initial iso](1980_initialIso.md) peer records the library names for the isomorphism and uniqueness lemmas.

<!-- formalization -->

**Theorem (`proposition_66`).** Every homomorphism from an initial algebra agrees with the canonical homomorphism furnished by initiality.

*Proof.* Invoke uniqueness of homomorphisms from an initial algebra. ∎
